==== Easy and exhaustive way but without serial ====
The general idea is here to upload the *-brn-squashfs-factory.bin through [[docs:techref:bootloader:brnboot#recovery_web_interface]], which results in a usable OpenWrt router.

To have the full 16MB Flash available or to upgrade with a nor-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin image, one needs to flash the full 16MB NOR flash 
(I tried flashing gluon directly, but it showed that the device arcadyan_vgv7510kw22-brn can't be upgraded with arcadyan_vgv7510kw22-nor image).

Therefore a 16MB firmware image is created based on the nor-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin and your specific board_config, which makes the device compatible with other sysupgrade images.

The partition backup is also possible through the OpenWrt [[docs:guide-user:troubleshooting:backup_restore#back_up]] UI.

The 16MB firmware image is then flashed through the hidden recovery web interface.

extensive Forum Thread: [[https://forum.lede-project.org/t/installing-lede-u-boot-via-brnboot-web-interface-without-rs232/9857/6|Installing LEDE/u-boot via brnboot web interface (without rs232)]]

This Forum link helped me understand the [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/difference-between-nor-and-brn/7880/3|Difference between NOR and BRN images]]

==== Easy & short guide (serial + TFTP) ====

based on: [[toh:arcadyan:arv7506pw11#installation|Arcadyan ARV7506PW11 (Alice IAD 4421 / o2 Box 4421)]]

  - Before permanently flashing U-Boot and OpenWrt on your router you should [[toh:arcadyan:vgv7510kw22#create_a_backup_of_the_original_firmwareflash_contents|backup as explained here]].
  - For the Backups and the upcoming permanent flashing of U-Boot you always need to start from U-Boot loaded in the memory which can either be done by [[toh:arcadyan:vgv7510kw22#booting_via_brnboot_noninvasive|"Booting via brnboot"]] or [[toh:arcadyan:vgv7510kw22#booting_via_uart|"Booting via UART"]].
  - Then you can [[toh:arcadyan:vgv7510kw22#flash_u-boot|permanently flash U-Boot via TFTP]].
  - After U-Boot is permanently installed on NOR flash you can [[toh:arcadyan:vgv7510kw22#flash_openwrt|flash OpenWrt via TFTP]].

